60,3,1,talk,May,,"@All, the options are here. A: Rotating Location. B: Managed Collection Hours. C: Enclosed Structure. Let’s vote.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"@May, I have reviewed the options. Given the physical constraints and the station block’s failure, I strongly advise against C.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Mizuki, agreed. C is too expensive and slow. I’m leaning toward B, but I worry about who actually does the watching.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Midori,,"@Kenji, I worry about the watching too. But A is impossible for the narrow frontage, and C is a trap. I’m leaning B, hoping we can share the burden gently.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Servas,,"@Kenji, the watching is the true cost. I have seen the minutes; their structure failed because the burden was uneven. I vote for B, but only if the rotation is fair.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,May,,"@Servas, fair rotation is non-negotiable. I vote B, but only if the gate household is explicitly protected from the heaviest shifts.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@May, I agree. The ninety-centimetre frontage makes A impossible, and C is a trap. I vote B, provided the oversight is strictly rotated so no one is stuck.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@May, I vote B. The ledger shows we bleed money on messes, so prevention is cheaper. But we must rotate the watching fairly, or it fails.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@May, I vote B. We must ensure the rotation is gentle so we don’t create new enemies. I want us to still be able to knock on each other’s doors.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@May, I vote B. Fairness in the rotation is the only way to preserve our peace. Let us proceed with this arrangement.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,May,,"@All, B has five votes. It is adopted. We will draft the rotation schedule to protect the gate household immediately.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,"- **Mizuki**: @May, agreed. I will draft the rotation schedule to ensure the narrow frontage is never burdened with oversight.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
